<title>FRANCE: Paris airports import traffic up 1.9pct in Jan 97.</title>
<headline>Paris airports import traffic up 1.9pct in Jan 97.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>January 1997 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 40,350 tonnes, an increase of 1.9 percent on the same month last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>January 1997 ADP import traffic in tonnes, by region, with percentage change on January 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p> Domestic		  2,472	down  5.8pct</p>
<p> European Union	  4,901	up    6.1</p>
<p> Non-EU Europe	     923	up   27.5</p>
<p> North Africa		862	down 34.4</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa    4,419	down  7.7</p>
<p> North America	  13,039	down  6.0</p>
<p> French territories	736	up   14.0</p>
<p> Latin America	   1,337	down  9.1</p>
<p> Middle East	     2,099	up    4.7</p>
<p> Far East		  9,561	up   26.6</p>
<p> Total		    40,350	up    1.9</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
